.TH FQDNCREDMGR 1 "2026-07-06" "a2tools 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fqdncredmgr \- manage registrar API credentials
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fqdncredmgr
.RB add " " \-p " " \fIprovider\fR " " \-u " " \fIusername\fR
.RB [ \-k " " \fB\-\fR ]
.B fqdncredmgr
.RB update " " \-p " " \fIprovider\fR " " \-u " " \fIusername\fR
.RB [ \-k " " \fB\-\fR ]
.B fqdncredmgr
.RB delete " " \-p " " \fIprovider\fR
.B fqdncredmgr
.RB list
.B fqdncredmgr
.RB { \-\-help " | " \-h }
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfqdncredmgr\fR stores registrar API credentials in a root\-only
SQLite database at \fB/var/lib/a2tools/creds.db\fR (mode 0600). The
credentials are read directly by \fBfqdnmgr\fR(1) from that database
\- there is no daemon, no socket and no environment variable
intermediary.
.PP
All arguments are named flags. Positional arguments are not accepted;
\fIPROVIDER\fR must be passed via \fB\-p\fR / \fB\-\-provider\fR and
\fIUSERNAME\fR via \fB\-u\fR / \fB\-\-username\fR.
.PP
Supplying the API key:
.IP
\fB\-k\fR \fB\-\fR   read the key from stdin (recommended for scripting)
.IP
omitted   prompt interactively with masked input
(\fBsystemd\-ask\-password\fR if available, otherwise \fBread \-s\fR
from \fB/dev/tty\fR).
.PP
Passing the key as a bare command\-line argument is NOT supported: argv
is visible to every local user via \fBps\fR and lands in shell
history.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B add
Add (or replace) credentials for a provider.
Requires \fB\-p\fR and \fB\-u\fR.
.TP
.B update
Replace the API key for an existing credential.
Requires \fB\-p\fR and \fB\-u\fR.
.TP
.B delete
Delete credentials for a provider.
Requires \fB\-p\fR.
.TP
.B list
List stored providers and masked usernames.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-provider " " \fIPROVIDER\fR
Provider plugin name (e.g. \fBnamecheap.com\fR).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-username " " \fIUSERNAME\fR
API username for the provider.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-api\-key " " \fB\-
Read the API key from stdin. Omit \fB\-k\fR to be prompted.
The key itself is NEVER accepted as a command\-line argument.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the embedded usage text and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Add credentials for \fBnamecheap.com\fR (interactive prompt):
.RS
.nf
sudo fqdncredmgr add -p namecheap.com -u <username>
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add credentials non\-interactively from a shell variable (key never
appears in argv or history):
.RS
.nf
printf '%s\n' "$KEY" | sudo fqdncredmgr add -p namecheap.com -u <username> -k \-
.fi
.RE
.PP
Delete credentials:
.RS
.nf
sudo fqdncredmgr delete -p namecheap.com
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/a2tools/creds.db
SQLite database with provider credentials.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/a2tools/providers/ ,
.I /etc/a2tools/providers/
Provider plugin directories (shipped and local overrides).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fqdnmgr (1),
.BR a2sitemgr (1)
.PP
Project homepage:
